   H. Derrien, A. Courcelle, L. C. Leal, N. Larson (ORNL)         9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
                ----- SUMMARY -----                               9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
   The ENDF/B-VII evaluation is a complete revision of almost all 9237 1451     
the data in the 238U evaluation. Major features of the evaluation 9237 1451     
are:                                                              9237 1451     
1. A new evaluation of the (n,f) cross section based on the       9237 1451     
   ENDF/B-VII standard cross section analysis is incorporated.    9237 1451     
2. New resolved resonance parameter data are incorporated.        9237 1451     
3. A new analysis of the prompt fission neutron spectrum matrix   9237 1451     
   based on the Los Alamos model is used to calculate neutron     9237 1451     
   spectra at all incident energies.                              9237 1451     
4. Improved delayed neutron data are incorporated.                9237 1451     
5. A new theoretical analysis utilizing coupled-channels optical  9237 1451     
   model and reaction theory calculations was performed and used  9237 1451     
   with experimental data to provide new scattering cross         9237 1451     
   sections and angular distributions.                            9237 1451     
6. The reaction theory calculations are utilized for (n,xn) and   9237 1451     
   other reactions.                                               9237 1451     
7. New calculations with coupled-channels optical model           9237 1451     
   parameters are used to extend direct reaction cross sections   9237 1451     
   and angular distributions to an excitation energy of 3.9 MeV.  9237 1451     
8. Improved fission energy release values are incorporated.       9237 1451     
9. A covariance evaluation was performed in the resolved energy   9237 1451     
   region (1.0-5 eV to 20.0 keV) at ORNL and above 20.0 keV at    9237 1451     
   LANL.                                                          9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
             ----- DETAILED DESCRIPTION -----                     9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
>> MF=1 GENERAL INFORMATION                                       9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
MT=452: TOTAL AVERAGE NEUTRON MULTIPLICITY PER FISSION (TOTAL     9237 1451     
        NUBAR)                                                    9237 1451     
   Sum of MT=455 and 456.                                         9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
MT=455: AVERAGE DELAYED NEUTRON MULTIPLICITY PER FISSION          9237 1451     
   Based on new delayed neutron 6-group parameters from CINDER'90 9237 1451     
summation calculations.  The CINDER calculations (Wi05) are based 9237 1451     
on a new CINDER library in which beta-decay half-lives and beta-  9237 1451     
delayed neutron-emission probablities are obtained from the       9237 1451     
evaluated experimental data file NuBase2003 (Au03), when          9237 1451     
available there. When experimental data are not available, the    9237 1451     
data are calculated using a model where allowed Gamow-Teller      9237 1451     
decays are treated in a microscopic quasi-particle random-phase   9237 1451     
approximation (QRPA) and the first forbidden decays are treated   9237 1451     
in the statistical gross theory (Mo03). The data were             9237 1451     
extrapolated to 30 MeV.                                           9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
MT=456: AVERAGE PROMPT NEUTRON MULTIPLICITY PER FISSION           9237 1451     
   1.e-5 eV - 30 MeV:  Taken from the ENDF/B-VI evaluation,       9237 1451     
except nubar was extended to 30 MeV. Values above 4-6 MeV were    9237 1451     
renormalized to match the ENDF/B-VII standard 252Cf nubar value.  9237 1451     
The values below 6 MeV were left at the ENDF/B-VI values because  9237 1451     
of good agreement with fast criticals. The new evaluation agrees  9237 1451     
generally with exp. data within errors. The original ENDF/B-VI    9237 1451     
evaluation is based on an evaluation by Frehaut (Fr86), with an   9237 1451     
approximate correction for ENDF/B-VI standards. That evaluation   9237 1451     
made use of the experimental database, especially the extensive   9237 1451     
measurements of Frehaut et al. (Fr80).                            9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
MT=458:  ENERGY RELEASE FROM FISSION                              9237 1451     
   Modifications were made to MT=458 based on a new analysis by   9237 1451     
Madland (Ma06). The average total fission product kinetic energy  9237 1451     
(EFR) and the average total prompt fission gamma-ray energy (EGP) 9237 1451     
were taken from the Madland analysis. The average total prompt    9237 1451     
fission neutron kinetic energy (ENP) was obtained from NJOY,      9237 1451     
using the MF=5,MT=18 fission neutron spectra and prompt nubar     9237 1451     
(MT=1,MT=456) from the evaluation. (This value of total neutron   9237 1451     
energy is close to Madland's result.) The kinetic energy of       9237 1451     
delayed fission neutrons (END), the total energy from delayed     9237 1451     
gamma rays (EGD), the total energy released by delayed betas      9237 1451     
(EB), and the energy released by neutrinos (ENU) were carried     9237 1451     
over from the ENDF/B-VI evaluation. The total energy release per  9237 1451     
fission is: ET = EFR+ENP+END+EGP+EGD+EB+ENU, and the quantity ER  9237 1451     
(total energy less the neutrino energy, or pseudo-Q value) is     9237 1451     
simply ET-ENU. ER is also included as the fission Q-value in      9237 1451     
MF=3, MT=18,19,20,21,38.                                          9237 1451     
   The uncertainties in EFR, ENP, END, EGP, EGD, EB, ENU, ER, and 9237 1451     
ET are carried over from ENDF/B-VI.                               9237 1451     
   There is currently no format for including energy dependence   9237 1451     
in the ENDF/B file.  These are included in the NJOY processing.   9237 1451     
