>> MF=5 ENERGY DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES               9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
MT=18: PROMPT FISSION NEUTRON SPECTRUM MATRIX                     9237 1451     
   Prompt fission neutron spectrum matrix for the n + 238U system 9237 1451     
was calculated (Ma02) using the Los Alamos (Madland-Nix) model    9237 1451     
(MN82) in its exact formulation with energy-dependent compound    9237 1451     
nucleus formation cross sections for the inverse processes. The   9237 1451     
matrix includes first-, second-, third-, and fourth-chance        9237 1451     
fission components and also includes the neutrons emitted prior   9237 1451     
to fission in second-, third-, and fourth-chance fission. The     9237 1451     
tabulated distribution law (LF=1) is used.                        9237 1451     
   The matrix contains vectors (spectra) for 24 incident neutron  9237 1451     
energies inducing the fission. These are:                         9237 1451     
        0.0 0.5 1.0 1.5 2.0 2.5 3.0 4.0 5.0 6.0 7.0 8.0 9.0 10.0  9237 1451     
        11.0 12.0 13.0 14.0 15.0 16.0 17.0 18.0 19.0 20.0 MeV     9237 1451     
   Until more experimental data become available, spectra for     9237 1451     
incident neutron energies above 20 MeV can be roughly             9237 1451     
approximated by using the 20 MeV spectrum.  An average over the   9237 1451     
spectra from 13 MeV to 18 MeV would be a better approximation.    9237 1451     
The 30-MeV spectrum in the evaluation is the same as the 20-MeV   9237 1451     
spectrum.                                                         9237 1451     
   The multiple-chance fission average prompt neutron             9237 1451     
multiplicity was calculated simultaneously and, in reproducing    9237 1451     
experiment, was important in determining the matrix.              9237 1451     
   The lowest incident neutron energy for a measured fission      9237 1451     
cross section for n + 238U is just under 2 eV with a value of     9237 1451     
about 5 microbarns.                                               9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
MT=455: DELAYED NEUTRON EMISSION SPECTRA FROM FISSION             9237 1451     
   The abundances are based on the new delayed-neutron            9237 1451     
calculations (Wi05) described under MF=1, MT=455. However, the    9237 1451     
earlier six-group spectra from ENDF/B-VI are carried over to      9237 1451     
ENDF/B-VII because new multigroup spectra have not yet been       9237 1451     
calculated with the new library.                                  9237 1451     
