>> MF=33 CROSS-SECTION COVARIANCE MATRICES                        9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
>>> MF=33 RESONANCE PARAMETER COVARIANCE (ORNL)                   9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
Resonance parameter covariance was generated in the resolved      9237 1451     
energy region (1.0-5 eV to 20.0 keV) with the computer code SAMMY 9237 1451     
at ORNL. Experimental data and uncertainties were used to generate9237 1451     
covariance data. SAMMY covariance information was converted in    9237 1451     
the ENDF FILE32 representation. However, because of computer      9237 1451     
storage concern the FILE32 was converted into the FILE33 (MT=1,   9237 1451     
2, 18, and 102) representation with reduced computer storage but  9237 1451     
approximating the features of the FILE32 representation. The full 9237 1451     
FILE32 matrices can be obtained directly from ORNL. The           9237 1451     
conversion was done with the PUFF-IV code. Above the unresolved   9237 1451     
resonance region (> 20.0 keV) covariance data were generated at   9237 1451     
LANL. Uncertainty on nubar was also generated at LANL.            9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
>>> MF=33 FAST-ENERGY COVARIANCE (LANL)                           9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
Cross-section covariance matrices in the fast energy region were  9237 1451     
obtained through a combination of nuclear reaction sensitivity    9237 1451     
calculations using the GNASH code, and available information on   9237 1451     
experimental uncertainties for some of the cross sections. The    9237 1451     
sensitivity of GNASH results on the choice of model parameters    9237 1451     
was assessed, and the KALMAN code (Ka97) was used to merge        9237 1451     
sensitivity calculations with experimental uncertainties.         9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
Prompt (MT456) and total (MT452) neutron multiplicity covariance  9237 1451     
matrices were obtained from a generalized least-squares study of  9237 1451     
experimental data alone, and no model calculation were used.      9237 1451     
                                                                  9237 1451     
More details on this work can be found in (Ta08).                 9237 1451     
